---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const tools = [
  { name: 'Daftra', status: 'Vendor says fully integrated with ETA (e-signature, GS1 codes, Egyptian VAT)', fit: 'Accounting / e-invoice SMEs', note: 'From $20/mo billed yearly (USD)', href: '/eg/daftra/' },
  { name: 'AccFlex', status: 'Vendor says ETA-approved; construction edition with مستخلصات', fit: 'SMEs incl. contractors', note: 'Not confirmed (quote form)', href: '/eg/accflex-erp/' },
  { name: 'DoubleClick ERP', status: 'Vendor says it sends مستخلصات (payment certificates) and invoices to the ETA directly', fit: 'Contractors (engineering → finance)', note: 'Quote-based', href: '/eg/doubleclick-erp/' },
  { name: 'Voko ERP', status: 'Separate ETA e-invoice module + مستخلصات in its contracting module', fit: 'Contractors', note: 'Quote-based', href: '/eg/voko-erp/' },
  { name: 'Edara', status: 'Egyptian e-invoicing in the Ultimate plan; vendor says it guides customers through ETA integration', fit: 'Trading and distribution SMEs', note: 'From $29/mo + $5/user billed yearly (USD); Ultimate $79 + $12/user', href: '/eg/edara-erp/' },
  { name: 'Odoo', status: 'Native ETA localization (API, GS1, USB e-sign), via partners', fit: 'Full ERP if you want one system', note: 'SaaS + implementation', href: '/eg/odoo/' },
  { name: 'OrchidaTax', status: 'ETA middleware/connector for SAP/Oracle/Dynamics/Odoo', fit: 'Keep your ERP, add compliance', note: 'Quote-based', href: '/eg/orchidatax/' },
  { name: 'QuickBooks', status: 'No ETA e-invoicing described by Intuit; needs a third-party connector (OrchidaTax lists QuickBooks)', fit: 'Firms already on QuickBooks', note: 'Connector priced separately', href: '/eg/quickbooks/' },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'Is ETA e-invoicing mandatory yet, and for whom?', a: `Yes, for the taxpayers named in ETA's phased decisions. ETA made e-invoicing mandatory in phases (phase 5 began on 15 December 2021, and phase 8 ran from September to December 2022), and its online inquiry tool shows whether a particular business is covered, so check your status there. B2C transactions are covered by the parallel e-receipt system. The VAT registration threshold has been under review since late 2025, so none is stated here.` },
  { q: 'What is the "clearance" model?', a: 'Egypt uses a real-time clearance (Continuous Transaction Control) model: each document is transmitted to the ETA and validated BEFORE it is issued to the recipient. The ETA checks the structure, tax math, e-seal and product codes, then assigns a UUID; rejected documents return error codes. B2C e-receipts carry a QR code for verification. This is stricter than post-audit reporting: the tax authority sees and approves each document in real time.' },
  { q: 'What happens if I don\'t comply?', a: 'Two consequences. (1) Non-compliant firms can be barred from dealing with government bodies and public tenders, and face import/export restrictions. (2) Penalties under Law 206/2020 (Article 71) range from EGP 20,000 to EGP 100,000 for failures to register or issue e-documents, with a tiered late-reporting escalation. Records must be kept at least 5 years.' },
  { q: 'What format and what\'s the legal basis?', a: 'Documents are structured JSON or XML (not PDF) per the ETA schema, with a UUID, a cryptographic hash, and a mandatory electronic signature via an approved certificate (HSM or USB token). Products are coded using GS1 (GTIN/GPC) or national EGS codes. The legal basis is the Unified Tax Procedures Law No. 206 of 2020 (Article 71 sets the fines), its Executive Regulations (Decree No. 286 of 2021), and the VAT Law No. 67 of 2016, administered by the Egyptian Tax Authority (ETA) under the Ministry of Finance.' },
  { q: 'Does my accounting software need to be ETA-native?', a: `If your business is covered by ETA's decisions, your software must reach the ETA somehow. Daftra, Edara (Ultimate plan), AccFlex, Namasoft and Voko say they submit to the ETA, DoubleClick says it sends مستخلصات and invoices directly, and Odoo has an Egyptian e-invoicing module. Intuit's global pages do not describe ETA e-invoicing for QuickBooks, so it needs a connector such as OrchidaTax, which lists QuickBooks among its integrations; Wafeq's Egypt pages make no ETA claim, so confirm with Wafeq. The right question for any vendor: "Do you clear documents through the ETA directly, or which connector do I need?"` },
  { q: 'What\'s the wider Egyptian tax context, and the FX angle?', a: 'The general VAT rate is 14%. For contractors, ETA lists Ministerial Decision 418/2025 on the tax basis for construction contracts, and October 2025 press reports describe 14% VAT being applied to contracting works, including existing contracts. Law 6/2025 gives tax incentives and simpler rules to projects with annual turnover up to EGP 20 million. On currency: Daftra, Edara, Odoo and PlanRadar list prices in USD, so their EGP cost moves with the exchange rate; Wafeq publishes EGP prices for Egypt.' },
];

const pageTitle = 'ETA E-Invoicing in Egypt: 2026 Guide for Contractors';
const pageDescription = `Egypt's ETA e-invoicing explained for the building trades: the legal basis, the real-time clearance model, who must comply under ETA's phased decisions, VAT on contracting works, and which tools say they submit to the ETA (incl. مستخلصات). Independent guide, updated September 2026.`;

const guideUrl = new URL('/eg/guides/eta-e-invoicing/', Astro.site).toString();
const arUrl = new URL('/eg/ar/guides/eta-e-invoicing/', Astro.site).toString();
const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Egypt', url: '/eg/' },
  { name: 'ETA e-invoicing for contractors', url: '/eg/guides/eta-e-invoicing/' },
];

const articleSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Article', headline: pageTitle, description: pageDescription,
  datePublished: '2026-06-20', dateModified: '2026-09-30', inLanguage: 'en',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'WrenchStack Research', url: 'https://wrenchstack.com/research/' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'WrenchStack', url: 'https://wrenchstack.com' },
  mainEntityOfPage: guideUrl,
};
const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
};
---

<Layout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} alternateUrls={[{ hreflang: 'en', href: guideUrl }, { hreflang: 'ar', href: arUrl }, { hreflang: 'x-default', href: guideUrl }]}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleSchema)} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <div class="mb-3 flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-orange-600">🇪🇬 Egypt · Compliance guide</p>
        <a href="/eg/ar/guides/eta-e-invoicing/" class="rounded-md border border-slate-300 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-50">العربية</a>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">
        ETA E-Invoicing in Egypt
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        What Egypt's national e-invoicing means for the building trades: it is mandatory for the taxpayers named in ETA's phased decisions. The clearance model, who must comply, the consequences, and which tools say they submit to the ETA (including مستخلصات).
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-500">By WrenchStack Research · Published June 2026, updated September 2026 · Not tax advice; confirm your situation with the ETA (eta.gov.eg) or your accountant.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="mb-8 rounded-lg border-2 border-orange-300 bg-orange-50 p-6">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">⏰ The short version</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-800 leading-relaxed">
        Egypt's <strong>ETA e-invoicing</strong> is <strong>mandatory in phases</strong>: it applies to the taxpayers named in ETA's phased decisions (phase 5 began on 15 December 2021; phase 8 ran from September to December 2022), and ETA's online inquiry tool shows whether your business is covered. It uses a real-time <strong>clearance</strong> model: each document validated by the Tax Authority <em>before</em> issuance (JSON/XML, UUID, mandatory e-signature). Fines under Law 206/2020 run <strong>EGP 20,000-100,000</strong>. The task: check your status, then make sure your tool clears to the ETA, directly or via a connector.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 text-center">
        <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Phased</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600">mandate by ETA decision; check with ETA's inquiry tool</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 text-center">
        <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">14%</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600">general VAT rate</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 text-center">
        <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Clearance</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600">validated before issue · UUID + e-sign</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10 prose prose-slate max-w-none">
      <h2>The timeline</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>15 Nov 2020:</strong> pilot: 134 large companies.</li>
        <li><strong>Feb-May 2021:</strong> waves extending to the Large Taxpayers Center.</li>
        <li><strong>1 Jul 2021:</strong> mandatory for sales to government / public sector (B2G).</li>
        <li><strong>15 Dec 2021:</strong> e-invoicing phase 5 began for the taxpayers named in ETA's decision.</li>
        <li><strong>Sep-Dec 2022:</strong> e-invoicing phase 8.</li>
        <li><strong>2022 → Jan 2025:</strong> the parallel B2C e-receipt system rolled out in successive taxpayer waves.</li>
        <li><strong>2025-2026:</strong> VAT and tax procedure laws amended again (including Law 149/2026); ETA lists Ministerial Decision 418/2025 on the tax basis for construction contracts; the VAT registration threshold has been under review since late 2025.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What the system requires</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Clearance, not reporting.</strong> Each document is transmitted to the ETA and validated <em>before</em> it is issued; without clearance and the assigned UUID, it isn't valid.</li>
        <li><strong>Structured format + e-signature.</strong> JSON or XML per the ETA schema, with a UUID, a cryptographic hash, and a mandatory electronic signature (HSM or USB token).</li>
        <li><strong>Product coding.</strong> GS1 (GTIN/GPC) or national EGS codes; B2C e-receipts carry a QR code.</li>
        <li><strong>Integration path.</strong> ETA API + SDK for larger firms, or a free web portal/desktop app for small ones, plus connectors (such as OrchidaTax) for tools without an ETA module. ETA publishes a list of service providers.</li>
        <li><strong>Check your scope.</strong> The mandate covers the taxpayers named in ETA's phased decisions; ETA's inquiry tool shows whether a business must use e-invoicing or e-receipts.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why this matters for contractors specifically</h2>
      <p>
        Contractors have their own tax points. ETA lists <strong>Ministerial Decision 418/2025</strong> on the tax basis for construction contracts, and October 2025 press reports describe <strong>14% VAT being applied to contracting works</strong>, including existing contracts. For <strong>مستخلصات (payment certificates)</strong>, <a href="/eg/doubleclick-erp/">DoubleClick</a> says it sends payment certificates and invoices to the ETA directly and prints the e-invoice QR code on the certificate, while <a href="/eg/voko-erp/">Voko</a>, Namasoft and AccFlex say their contracting modules handle payment certificates and that they support ETA e-invoicing. Check the currency too: Daftra, Edara and Odoo list prices in USD, so their EGP cost moves with the exchange rate.
      </p>

      <h2>The wider Egyptian tax context</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>VAT:</strong> standard <strong>14%</strong> (5% reduced in some cases; exports zero-rated).</li>
        <li><strong>Small projects:</strong> Law 6/2025 gives tax incentives and simpler rules to projects with annual turnover up to EGP 20 million.</li>
        <li><strong>The FX angle:</strong> the EGP is volatile and un-pegged, so USD-billed tools carry real currency risk for an EGP business.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Which tools are ETA-integrated?</h2>
      <p>
        From the software in our <a href="/eg/">Egypt directory</a>, here's how the tools relate to the ETA. Tools with an Egyptian e-invoicing module submit directly (Odoo has one through its Egyptian localization); tools without one, such as QuickBooks, need a connector. Always confirm current status with the vendor.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-sm border border-slate-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        <thead class="bg-slate-50 text-left text-slate-700">
          <tr>
            <th class="p-3 font-semibold">Tool</th>
            <th class="p-3 font-semibold">ETA status</th>
            <th class="p-3 font-semibold">Best fit</th>
            <th class="p-3 font-semibold">Pricing</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100 bg-white">
          {tools.map((t) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-slate-900"><a href={t.href} class="hover:text-orange-600">{t.name}</a></td>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-700">{t.status}</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-600">{t.fit}</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-600">{t.note}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-slate-500">ETA status reflects what each vendor says, as checked in September 2026; confirm current ETA integration directly with each vendor.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 p-6">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">The one question to ask any vendor</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        Don't assume a good accounting tool clears to the ETA. And if you're a contractor, ask about مستخلصات too. Ask: <strong>"Do you clear documents through the ETA directly, do you handle مستخلصات, and do you price in EGP or USD?"</strong> A vague answer is your signal. If you're on QuickBooks, plan for a connector such as OrchidaTax, which lists QuickBooks among its integrations.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="mb-5 text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3">
        {faqs.map((f) => (
          <details class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-slate-900">{f.q}</summary>
            <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">{f.a}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 p-5 text-xs text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">
      <strong class="text-slate-700">Sources &amp; verification:</strong> First verified June 2026 from PwC, Sovos, VATupdate, EDICOM, SNI and Comarch, cross-checked against the ETA; mandate phases, VAT and contracting-tax points re-checked against ETA's Arabic website in September 2026. Legal basis: Unified Tax Procedures Law No. 206 of 2020 (Art. 71), Executive Regulations Decree No. 286 of 2021, VAT Law No. 67 of 2016, amended again in 2025 and 2026 (including Law 149/2026). Real-time clearance/CTC, JSON/XML + UUID + mandatory e-signature and the penalty range EGP 20,000-100,000 come from the June sources. The e-invoicing phase dates, Ministerial Decision 418/2025 and Law 6/2025 are from ETA's site; the general 14% VAT rate and its application to contracting works are from 2025-2026 press reports. The VAT registration threshold has been under review since late 2025, so none is stated here. The exact 2026 penalty-tier amounts are not stated here as they could not be confirmed against the current Arabic decree. General information, not tax advice. Spotted an error? <a href="/contact/" class="underline">Tell us</a> and we'll correct it.
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-lg bg-slate-900 p-8 text-white">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Compare Egyptian trades software & services</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">Independent reviews of ETA-ready Egyptian software, tender access, social-insurance payroll and Contractors All Risks insurance, with no pay-to-play.</p>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/eg/" class="rounded-md bg-orange-500 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-orange-600">🇪🇬 Egypt directory →</a>
        <a href="/eg/compare/" class="rounded-md bg-white px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 hover:bg-slate-100">Compare vendors</a>
        <a href="/for-vendors/" class="rounded-md border border-white/30 bg-white/10 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-white/20">Are you a vendor? Work with us</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
